{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5","id":1282916,"title":"Karsh in V5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-26T15:25:06-08:00","id":1282916,"title":"Karsh in V5","content":"I've got a question about Karsh's status in V5. In the Brujah Trilogy the Dux Bellorum of the Camarilla was staked and thrown into the ocean's depths by Theo Bell and it was revealed he was the servant of 2 more powerful vampires hiding in Rio de Janeiro, subsequently destroyed by a Sabbat-Camarilla combined strike team but not before they killed Xaviar, the former Gangrel Justicar. Before being defeated, Karsh killed several other kindred, including Theo Bell's sire, Don Cerro. These events happened right before Ghenna and may or might not have been erased by V5 new metaplot.<br /> In Short: is Karsh still around in V5 or did the events of the Brujah Trilogy happen and he's sleeping with the fishes?<br /> Here's what I know to be true in V5 regarding this matter:<br /> <br /> -Xaviar met and survived an encounter with something resembling the host bodies of the Tzimisce antediluvian and subsequently led the Gangrel out of the Camarilla.<br /> -Xaviar is dead, circumstances unknown, which seems to fit his death at the hands of Karsh &quot;puppetmasters&quot;.<br /> -Theo Bell did a whole lot of stuff for a 9th generation ancilla however powerful. He almost killed Vitel (a 5th generation lasombra methuselah), he killed Hardestadt the younger and led the Brujah out of the Camarilla (it's stated he's still acting as a mediator between the Camarilla and the Anarchs, how could that even be possible after what he did in the Convention of Prague I really can't fathom).<br /> <br /> All of this doesn't help much to determine Karsh's fate. Is there information of some kind I am missing? And besides what about Karsh's &quot;puppetmasters&quot;? It was never revealed who or what they were. Just 2 extremely powerful kindred, one male and one female, possibly working for the antediluvians and iirc being infernalists. Since they were Karsh's masters I always assumed they were of the 4th generation. Any ideas about their identity?<br /> <br /> Lastly there's the matter of Karsh's true identity as well. There are 2 prominent theories about it. One is that he was originally a 4th generation gangrel who used the Dual Form Protean power (lvl 9) and split himself into 2 different bodies (Karsh and Jalan-Aajav) the other, which I favor is he was Qarakh, an Anda Gangrel from the Dark Ages who diablerized the Ventrue methuselah Alexander and then impersonated both &quot;Karsh&quot; and &quot;Jalan-Aajav&quot; as 2 different vampires placed at the very top of both the Sabbat and the Camarilla. The Brujah Trilogy seemed to favor this theory since after Karsh was defeated Jalan-Aajav disappeared as well with no explanation whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":".  Corrected wrong information about some events from the Brujah Trilogy 01-26-2019, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T17:46:54-08:00","id":1282932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5#post1282916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question about Karsh's status in V5. In the Brujah Trilogy the Dux Bellorum of the Camarilla was staked and thrown into the ocean's depths by Theo Bell and it was revealed he was the servant of 2 more powerful vampires hiding in Rio de Janeiro, subsequently destroyed by a Sabbat-Camarilla combined strike team but not before they killed Xaviar, the former Gangrel Justicar. Before being defeated, Karsh killed several other kindred, including Theo Bell's sire, Don Cerro. These events happened right before Ghenna and may or might not have been erased by V5 new metaplot.<br /> In Short: is Karsh still around in V5 or did the events of the Brujah Trilogy happen and he's sleeping with the fishes?<br /> Here's what I know to be true in V5 regarding this matter:<br /> <br /> -Xaviar met and survived an encounter with something resembling the host bodies of the Tzimisce antediluvian and subsequently led the Gangrel out of the Camarilla.<br /> -Xaviar is dead, circumstances unknown, which seems to fit his death at the hands of Karsh &quot;puppetmasters&quot;.<br /> -Theo Bell did a whole lot of stuff for a 9th generation ancilla however powerful. He almost killed Vitel (a 5th generation lasombra methuselah), he killed Hardestadt the younger and led the Brujah out of the Camarilla (it's stated he's still acting as a mediator between the Camarilla and the Anarchs, how could that even be possible after what he did in the Convention of Prague I really can't fathom).<br /> <br /> All of this doesn't help much to determine Karsh's fate. Is there information of some kind I am missing? And besides what about Karsh's &quot;puppetmasters&quot;? It was never revealed who or what they were. Just 2 extremely powerful kindred, one male and one female, possibly working for the antediluvians and iirc being infernalists. Since they were Karsh's masters I always assumed they were of the 4th generation. Any ideas about their identity?<br /> <br /> Lastly there's the matter of Karsh's true identity as well. There are 2 prominent theories about it. One is that he was originally a 4th generation gangrel who used the Dual Form Protean power (lvl 9) and split himself into 2 different bodies (Karsh and Jalan-Aajav) the other, which I favor is he was Qarakh, an Anda Gangrel from the Dark Ages who diablerized the Ventrue methuselah Alexander and then impersonated both &quot;Karsh&quot; and &quot;Jalan-Aajav&quot; as 2 different vampires placed at the very top of both the Sabbat and the Camarilla. The Brujah Trilogy seemed to favor this theory since after Karsh was defeated Jalan-Aajav disappeared as well with no explanation whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>For all intents and purposes, Karsh would still be sleeping with the fishes. Jalan-Aajav is presented as a separate character, and is dead in V5, a casualty of the origin of the SI.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T20:03:56-08:00","id":1282946,"title":"","content":"I maintain that Karsh and Jalan are the same character but rather than the Protean 9 split, it was more the two made use of a lot of body doubles and Obfuscate-capable minions.<br /> <br /> So are they dead?<br /> <br /> Who knows.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T20:09:15-08:00","id":1282949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1282946#post1282946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I maintain that Karsh and Jalan are the same character but rather than the Protean 9 split, it was more the two made use of a lot of body doubles and Obfuscate-capable minions.<br /> <br /> So are they dead?<br /> <br /> Who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Has anyone ever seen them in the same place, at the same time? As for them being dead, (A) that depends on the individual storyteller and (B) since when has being dead ever stopped anyone in the WoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T21:32:11-08:00","id":1282959,"title":"","content":"I take that they are the same Cainite, therefore, if Jalan is dead, so is Karsh.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T21:34:46-08:00","id":1282960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <st