<i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T03:38:33-08:00","id":1283005,"title":"","content":"I like the Anda Theory. In my Headcanon they were Anda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T06:12:52-08:00","id":1283024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1282964#post1282964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, I like to think the SI were led to him by the True Black Hand.<br /> <br /> BJD is like, &quot;Karsh is going to whoop the True Hand's ass! BOOYA!&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm like, &quot;The guys whose whole thing [aside from being ridiculous] is they are the world's best manipulators are going to be beaten by the guy who exists solely for battle? I don't think so.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>About the Tal'mahe'ra leading the SI to Jalan-Aajav:<br /> <br /> -We need to establish if Jalan-Ajav and Karsh were one and the same. If not then the SI killing J-A doesn't mean Karsh is dead too.<br /> -If they were one and the same and J-A really is dead then we need to believe a bunch of well equipped mortals (a couple dozen of them?) were able to put down a veritable monster way stronger and faster than a human being could ever hope to be and with senses so keen to be considered superhuman. That seems unlikely but could have happened. In that case Karsh and A-J were the same vampire but the SI killed him off. The events of the Brujah trilogy did not happen. The &quot;puppetmasters&quot; may or may not be real and Xaviar was likely killed by someone else.<br /> -If they were the same vampire and the SI did not really kill A-J then the question is: who did the SI really kill? Going with the theory that Karsh and J-A are two fake identities used by the same vampire (Qarakh?) then it stands to reason said vampire is a master manipulator, more likely than not to have powerful patrons helping him deceive both of the main sects while operating right near the top of their respective hierarchies. For such a vampire getting someone to use vicissitude/dominate to create an expendable body double of himself would have been trivial. If that's true then Karsh/Jalan-Aajav is still out there operating on his own unscrutable agenda, possibly on the oprders of his mysterious &quot;masters&quot;. In this case the events of the Brujah Trilogy may have happened in V5 but in a slightly different manner than what was written in the books (the Sabbat did not know about Jalan-Aajav supposed death and just mentioned he was nowhere to be found after Karsh was thrown into the ocean).<br /> -What about the &quot;puppetmasters&quot;? Reading the novels one of them was assumed to be &quot;True Brujah&quot; (note that in my headcanon they are fake and the progeny of Troile, which is not the Brujah antediluvian but &quot;just&quot; a 4th gen of comparable power to Ur-Shulgi and the creator of the &quot;True Brujah&quot; bloodline) the other could use balefire which is a Daimonion power which in turn morelikely than not means &quot;Baali&quot;. In the novels, iirc they were servants of the Antediluvians who wanted to facilitate their return and avoid being eaten in the process. That to me seemed like they actually were Tal'mahe'ra because that's basically what the True Black Hand wants to do. In the novels they killed Xaviar and in V5 Xaviar is dead, so it seems possible the events of the novels transpired as told.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Anda Theory. In my Headcanon they were Anda.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Agree, especially because Qarakh (which I believe to be the vampire behind the Karsh/Jalan-Aajav facade) used powers typical of the Anda. Yet it must be said the books list his grandsire Oderic as Gangrel. He won the right to embrace Aajav (Qarakh's sire) by challenging the Anda elder who ruled over Aajav and Qarakh's tribe and killing him. Also, all Anda were wiped out after the Wan-Quei used their progenitor, Dobrul, to lure them all in the same place and then destroyed them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T07:49:49-08:00","id":1283040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1283024#post1283024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -We need to establish if Jalan-Ajav and Karsh were one and the same. If not then the SI killing J-A doesn't mean Karsh is dead too.<br /> -If they were one and the same and J-A really is dead then we need to believe a bunch of well equipped mortals (a couple dozen of them?) were able to put down a veritable monster way stronger and faster than a human being could ever hope to be and with senses so keen to be considered superhuman. That seems unlikely but could have happened. In that case Karsh and A-J were the same vampire but the SI killed him off. The events of the Brujah trilogy did not happen. The &quot;puppetmasters&quot; may or may not be real and Xaviar was likely killed by someone else.</div> </div> </div> </div>On point one, I don't know that any book ever posited that they were the same person, nor did any book explicitly state they were not. They were written as separate characters, but hints about, but nothing has ever been flatly stated 'this is what happened and they are both the same person'. It's a tidbit for players to play with. But V5 explicitly posits J-A as dead, and that would effect your game based on how you, as ST, choose to run their existence.<br /> <br /> On point two, this discussion is getting old. The Masquerade literally exists because humans were killing vampires and the elders of the clans were throwing their childer at them in order to save their own skins. This was in the days of torches, pitchforks, swords and armor and True Faith. Human technology now is much more threatening than torches and pitchforks, and the SI is inherently backed by a lot of knowledge provided by the Society of Leopold. It's not like 'lol one dude went in and killed Jalan-Aajav'. They don't detail it, but man, think in terms of LOGIC of how the SI would deal with that. Go in during the day, when they know vampires have trouble (Even if they don't know about the limits of dice, they know sunlight fucks them up), in groups, as a counter-terror unit. OR even a fucking SWAT unit to justify the use of the type of arms they would need to.<br /> <br /> It's not unrealistic and entirely possible and plausible, unless your outlook on vampires is 'lol old vampires are so much above humans no amount of humans or human technology can be a threat!' but, at that point, you're invalidating the entire reason the Masquerade was created and continues to exist. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T07:50:41-08:00","id":1283041,"title":"","content":"I always thought it was lame though how they genocides the Anda. It made more sense to me if they were decimated instead. I mean you don\u2019t kill the Survivor clan that easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T08:18:13-08:00","id":1283051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1283024#post1283024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-If they were one and the same and J-A really is dead then we need to believe a bunch of well equipped mortals (a couple dozen of them?) were able to put down a veritable monster way stronger and faster than a human being could ever hope to be and with senses so keen to be considered superhuman. That seems unlikely but could have happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are fighting fair, you are doing it wrong.<br /> <br /> Why do you assume a SI team tangled with JA/K? The smart thing would have been to fire bomb where ever he was sleeping - unless he was bonded to the Earth, then they dig him up with a bulldozer and firebomb him. And any SI team would have been armed with dragons breath and other weapons for burning a mother fucker.<br /> <br /> Also, in terms of that Gangrel power that splits one person into two; what happens if one of them dies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T08:21:13-08:00","id":1283052,"title":"","content":"Random aside:<br /> <br /> My canonical True Brujah are the descendants of Brujah....but Brujah only had Troile as a descendant.<br /> <br /> The True Brujah are an ancestor cult that rejected Troile after Carthage and developed Temporis as an Alternate Power on Celerity in rebellion to her infernalism.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T09:24:57-08:00","id":1283065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thebiglarpnerd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1283040#post1283040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On point one, I don't know that any book ever posited that they were the same person, nor did any book explicitly state they were not. They were written as separate characters, but hints about, but nothing has ever been flatly stated 'this is what happened and they are both the same person'. It's a tidbit for players to play with. But V5 explicitly posits J-A as dead, and that would effect your game based on how you, as ST, choose to run their existence.<br /> <br /> On point two, this discussion is getting old. The Masquerade literally exists because humans were killing vampires and the elders of the clans were throwing their childer at them in order to save their own skins. This was in the days of torches, pitchforks, swords and armor and True Faith. Human technology now is much more threatening than torches and pitchforks, and the SI is inherently backed by a lot of knowledge provided by the Society of Leopold. It's not like 'lol one dude went in and killed Jalan-Aajav'. They don't detail it, but man, think in terms of LOGIC of how the SI would deal with that. Go in during the day, when they know vampires have trouble (Even if they don't know about the limits of dice, they know sunlight fucks them up), in groups, as a counter-terror unit. OR even a fucking SWAT unit to justify the use of the type of arms they would need to.<br /> <br /> It's not unrealistic and entirely possible and plausible, unless your outlook on vampires is 'lol old vampires are so much above humans no amount of humans or human technology can be a threat!' but, at that point, you're invalidating the entire reason the Masquerade was created and continues to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>-Karsh and Jalan-Aajav were 2 vampires with the exact same stats, filling similar roles in 2 different sects and having somewhat similar backstories (but supposedly different ages). You are right it was never outright stated they were one and the same but I think it fair to say that possibility was strongly implied.<br /> -Of course. The best strategy for mortal hunters to deal with vampires is to act by daylight, when most vampires are sleeping or are weakened. If that's how you want a creature like Jalan-Aajav to die then that works. It's a good way to show how dangerous the SI really is (if taking out Mithras, which happened by night, and the Council of 7 weren't enough). I pointed out that Karsh/Jalan-Aajav, if he really was a single individual, had all the resources to fake his own death and it stands to reason what the SI really killed was not him but a patsy he set up.<br /> -The point above is reinforced by the fact Karsh had 2 masters, probably True Black Hand. He obviously was an important asset for them and they had all the resources needed to help him prepare for the SI strike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T10:03:19-08:00","id":1283073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1283065#post1283065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Karsh and Jalan-Aajav were 2 vampires with the exact same stats, filling similar roles in 2 different sects and having somewhat similar backstories (but supposedly different ages). You are right it was never outright stated they were one and the same but I think it fair to say that possibility was strongly implied.<br /> -Of course. The best strategy for mortal hunters to deal with vampires is to act by daylight, when most vampires are sleeping or are weakened. If that's how you want a creature like Jalan-Aajav to die then that works. It's a good way to show how dangerous the SI really is (if taking out Mithras, which happened by night, and the Council of 7 weren't enough). I pointed out that Karsh/Jalan-Aajav, if he really was a single individual, had all the resources to fake his own death and it stands to reason what the SI really killed was not him but a patsy he set up.<br /> -The point above is reinforced by the fact Karsh had 2 masters, probably True Black Hand. He obviously was an important asset for them and they had all the resources needed to help him prepare for the SI strike.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And its your game to do what you want with, but you asked about Karsh in V5, and so we've presented:<br /> - Nothing ever said they were the same person in any edition.<br /> - V5 states Jalan-Aajav is dead in a letter on pg 29 on the core book, which is the only mention that he gets so far.<br /> - V5 hasn't mentioned Karsh at all.<br /> <br /> So otherwise you have to extrapolate from it how you want it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5704-thebiglarpnerd","name":"thebiglarpnerd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T11:37:22-08:00","id":1283083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1283005#post1283005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the Anda Theory. In my Headcanon they were Anda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Therefore they we're two different Cainites... hmm. How on earth we're their stats and (mostly) Backgrounds exactly the same? Twins? Even split body would have at least one stat different.<br /> <br /> My head canon was that when Matasuntha went after civilization, her horde killed a favored one of the Clever Prince, so he splitted the mind of her favored childe in return.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T11:59:31-08:00","id":1283086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1283065#post1283065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Karsh and Jalan-Aajav were 2 vampires with the exact same stats, filling similar roles in 2 different sects and having somewhat similar backstories (but supposedly different ages). You are right it was never outright stated they were one and the same but I think it fair to say that possibility was strongly implied.<br /> -Of course. The best strategy for mortal hunters to deal with vampires is to act by daylight, when most vampires are sleeping or are weakened. If that's how you want a creature like Jalan-Aajav to die then that works. It's a good way to show how dangerous the SI really is (if taking out Mithras, which happened by night, and the Council of 7 weren't enough). I pointed out that Karsh/Jalan-Aajav, if he really was a single individual, had all the resources to fake his own death and it stands to reason what the SI really killed was not him but a patsy he set up.<br /> -The point above is reinforced by the fact Karsh had 2 masters, probably True Black Hand. He obviously was an important asset for them and they had all the resources needed to help him prepare for the SI strike.</div> </div> </div> </div>Karsh/Jalan was strongly suggested being the same by the fiction universe in revised (I think it was Phillipe Boulle the developer of the line IIRC) so too his appearance in Brujah trilogy by Tim Pedopulos and Ari Marmell's The Final Night when Lucita tried to search for Jalan and he was (sort of) &quot;unavailable&quot; (due to what happened in BT3).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T12:05:08-08:00","id":1283087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1283041#post1283041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought it was lame though how they genocides the Anda. It made more sense to me if they were decimated instead. I mean you don\u2019t kill the Survivor clan that easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I take some survived (when did a Bloodline ever died?!) and there's Matasuntha... she simply disappeared when she made the Grand Gather to destroy human civilization... now that I think of it, it was during around the same time of the Feast of Folly and the attack of Samiel to the Tzimisce founder (around 700 a.d.). Did the Antediluvians went hothead and manipulated their childer into decimating themselves?!?!<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T12:09:58-08:00","id":1283088,"title":"","content":"Wait, so did the fight of The Dracon against Triglav. That happened soon before the embrace of Gesu, so yet another decimation within the clan.<br /> <br /> Interesting times indeed to storytell.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T14:10:23-08:00","id":1283117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1283087#post1283087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I take some survived (when did a Bloodline ever died?!) and there's Matasuntha... she simply disappeared when she made the Grand Gather to destroy human civilization... now that I think of it, it was during around the same time of the Feast of Folly and the attack of Samiel to the Tzimisce founder (around 700 a.d.). Did the Antediluvians went hothead and manipulated their childer into decimating themselves?!?!<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be honest all it would have taken for a few Anda to survive was for them to be in torpor or staked at the time the Wan-Quei enacted their ritual. They could not go back to their sire because they were simply unable to. So they might be &quot;dead&quot; as the Ravnos are after the week of nightmares.<br /> <br /> That said: Matasuntha called her Grand Gathering in 400 CE rampaged for a few years with the barbarian hordes who caused the Western Roman Empire fall, then went in torpor due to a battle with another powerful vampire. She reemerged around 900CE.<br /> <br /> As for Samiel and Tzimisce there's no certain date, it's possible it happened in the years before 700CE, IF it happened as the Tzimisce's claim, which is dubious, other sources place his death at the end of the Baali Wars for example, and that means a few thousand years before the birth of Christ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T20:08:37-08:00","id":1283176,"title":"","content":"If K-Dog were to reappear, I hope it would involve an answer about his relationship with Jalan-Aajav.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T21:09:28-08:00","id":1283185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1283117#post1283117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, to be honest all it would have taken for a few Anda to survive was for them to be in torpor or staked at the time the Wan-Quei enacted their ritual. They could not go back to their sire because they were simply unable to. So they might be &amp;quot;dead&amp;quot; as the Ravnos are after the week of nightmares.<br /> <br /> That said: Matasuntha called her Grand Gathering in 400 CE rampaged for a few years with the barbarian hordes who caused the Western Roman Empire fall, then went in torpor due to a battle with another powerful vampire. She reemerged around 900CE.<br /> <br /> As for Samiel and Tzimisce there's no certain date, it's possible it happened in the years before 700CE, IF it happened as the Tzimisce's claim, which is dubious, other sources place his death at the end of the Baali Wars for example, and that means a few thousand years before the birth of Christ.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Tzimisce civil war it was around that time prior to Gesu's embrace for sure and further info on the Dracon spawning the destroyed Antediluvian and then leaving it in Samisegetuza to the Ruthven lienage care is detailed in Myranda Kalis' Dark Ages Novel Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> And yeah, got the dates wrong of the Grand Gather, my mistake.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T13:12:35-08:00","id":1293869,"title":"","content":"According to Quawiyya el-Ghaduba (sp? ) backstory, Who would have been Samiels last childe, Samiel and the second Baali-War would have been around 636 CE, so basically the same time period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25099-athanasius","name":"Athanasius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-05T15:41:58-08:00","id":1294191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Athanasius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1293869#post1293869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to Quawiyya el-Ghaduba (sp? ) backstory, Who would have been Samiels last childe, Samiel and the second Baali-War would have been around 636 CE, so basically the same time period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is we don't have a precise date for the Baali Wars... or even the kind of conflicts they entailed.<br /> <br /> The first one is supposed to have happened at the time of the First OR Second City but the nature of the events is debated and contraddictory.<br /> <br /> The second one is supposed to have taken place around 1.500 BC and was supposedly won by blowing up the island of Thera.<br /> <br /> Some, like you do, also consider the Baali-Assamite war that happened in the 7th century CE to be the second Baali War, but it could also be the third. This might be the conflict that caused Samiel's death... or not.<br /> <br /> Bottom line: the Baali and their history is really hazy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T15:38:03-07:00","id":1404105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5#post1282916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question about Karsh's status in V5. In the Brujah Trilogy the Dux Bellorum of the Camarilla was staked and thrown into the ocean's depths by Theo Bell and it was revealed he was the servant of 2 more powerful vampires hiding in Rio de Janeiro, subsequently destroyed by a Sabbat-Camarilla combined strike team but not before they killed Xaviar, the former Gangrel Justicar. Before being defeated, Karsh killed several other kindred, including Theo Bell's sire, Don Cerro. These events happened right before Ghenna and may or might not have been erased by V5 new metaplot.<br /> In Short: is Karsh still around in V5 or did the events of the Brujah Trilogy happen and he's sleeping with the fishes?<br /> Here's what I know to be true in V5 regarding this matter:<br /> <br /> -Xaviar met and survived an encounter with something resembling the host bodies of the Tzimisce antediluvian and subsequently led the Gangrel out of the Camarilla.<br /> -Xaviar is dead, circumstances unknown, which seems to fit his death at the hands of Karsh &quot;puppetmasters&quot;.<br /> -Theo Bell did a whole lot of stuff for a 9th generation ancilla however powerful. He almost killed Vitel (a 5th generation lasombra methuselah), he killed Hardestadt the younger and led the Brujah out of the Camarilla (it's stated he's still acting as a mediator between the Camarilla and the Anarchs, how could that even be possible after what he did in the Convention of Prague I really can't fathom).<br /> <br /> All of this doesn't help much to determine Karsh's fate. Is there information of some kind I am missing? And besides what about Karsh's &quot;puppetmasters&quot;? It was never revealed who or what they were. Just 2 extremely powerful kindred, one male and one female, possibly working for the antediluvians and iirc being infernalists. Since they were Karsh's masters I always assumed they were of the 4th generation. Any ideas about their identity?<br /> <br /> Lastly there's the matter of Karsh's true identity as well. There are 2 prominent theories about it. One is that he was originally a 4th generation gangrel who used the Dual Form Protean power (lvl 9) and split himself into 2 different bodies (Karsh and Jalan-Aajav) the other, which I favor is he was Qarakh, an Anda Gangrel from the Dark Ages who diablerized the Ventrue methuselah Alexander and then impersonated both &quot;Karsh&quot; and &quot;Jalan-Aajav&quot; as 2 different vampires placed at the very top of both the Sabbat and the Camarilla. The Brujah Trilogy seemed to favor this theory since after Karsh was defeated Jalan-Aajav disappeared as well with no explanation whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24992_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24992\" data-vbnamecard=\"24992\">Haquim</a> Who were the Puppet-masters? I''l buy this novel next moth, but can you tell me what is written about them? They were hidden in Rio? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24990-irad-the-strong","name":"Irad the Strong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T04:27:07-07:00","id":1404218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irad the Strong</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1404105#post1404105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Who were the Puppet-masters? I''l buy this novel next moth, but can you tell me what is written about them? They were hidden in Rio? Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately who they were was never made clear. Iirc one made use of Balefire to kill Xaviar, so that would imply a daimonion user which likely means Baali. I seem to recall the other one being True Brujah but I should check the book out for confirmation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T10:16:35-07:00","id":1404253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5#post1282916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got a question about Karsh's status in V5. In the Brujah Trilogy the Dux Bellorum of the Camarilla was staked and thrown into the ocean's depths by Theo Bell and it was revealed he was the servant of 2 more powerful vampires hiding in Rio de Janeiro, subsequently destroyed by a Sabbat-Camarilla combined strike team but not before they killed Xaviar, the former Gangrel Justicar. Before being defeated, Karsh killed several other kindred, including Theo Bell's sire, Don Cerro. These events happened right before Ghenna and may or might not have been erased by V5 new metaplot.<br /> In Short: is Karsh still around in V5 or did the events of the Brujah Trilogy happen and he's sleeping with the fishes?<br /> Here's what I know to be true in V5 regarding this matter:<br /> <br /> -Xaviar met and survived an encounter with something resembling the host bodies of the Tzimisce antediluvian and subsequently led the Gangrel out of the Camarilla.<br /> -Xaviar is dead, circumstances unknown, which seems to fit his death at the hands of Karsh &quot;puppetmasters&quot;.<br /> -Theo Bell did a whole lot of stuff for a 9th generation ancilla however powerful. He almost killed Vitel (a 5th generation lasombra methuselah), he killed Hardestadt the younger and led the Brujah out of the Camarilla (it's stated he's still acting as a mediator between the Camarilla and the Anarchs, how could that even be possible after what he did in the Convention of Prague I really can't fathom).<br /> <br /> All of this doesn't help much to determine Karsh's fate. Is there information of some kind I am missing? And besides what about Karsh's &quot;puppetmasters&quot;? It was never revealed who or what they were. Just 2 extremely powerful kindred, one male and one female, possibly working for the antediluvians and iirc being infernalists. Since they were Karsh's masters I always assumed they were of the 4th generation. Any ideas about their identity?<br /> <br /> Lastly there's the matter of Karsh's true identity as well. There are 2 prominent theories about it. One is that he was originally a 4th generation gangrel who used the Dual Form Protean power (lvl 9) and split himself into 2 different bodies (Karsh and Jalan-Aajav) the other, which I favor is he was Qarakh, an Anda Gangrel from the Dark Ages who diablerized the Ventrue methuselah Alexander and then impersonated both &quot;Karsh&quot; and &quot;Jalan-Aajav&quot; as 2 different vampires placed at the very top of both the Sabbat and the Camarilla. The Brujah Trilogy seemed to favor this theory since after Karsh was defeated Jalan-Aajav disappeared as well with no explanation whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Those involved in writing VtM at that time (and afterwards too) disliked the events of Brujah Trilogy and ignored most of it. Too bad, I liked the idea of Meonia, Rodrigo and Claudia as antagonists, plus the idea that Bell commited diablerie while completely insane due to the overseer's Dementation. Karsh killing Don Cerro, the fight between Bell and Xaviar against Karsh, and the death of the ex-justicar Gangrel were really good additions to the metaplot.<br /> <br /> Here's info from the writer's site about the NPCs:<br /> <br /> DELPHINE DECOURT<br /> <br /> Delphine was arguably the most important character to get right in Slave Ring. Although Theo is the 'Hero' -- that's combined Viewpoint Character and Protagonist for those of you into technical definitions -- Delphine is a vital part of the book's dynamic, a humanizing foil for Theo (who, let's face it, is quite a hard-ass) and also the character who acts as our window onto Kindred society, because it's all so fresh for her. All those things combine to make her really critical. I have whole swathes of mental notes about her, and I will take the time to write her up properly (if anyone seems in the least interested, anyway!), but for the moment I'm going to have to make do with just putting up some little bits and pieces.<br /> <br /> Delphine and Nathalie are seventeen, and would certainly have described themselves as pretty normal before Slave Ring kicked off. They're really close, do pretty much everything together, tell each other absolutely everything, and think in much the same way. Unlike some identical twins, they don't finish each other's sentences, but because they're on the same wavelength, they often use obscure symbology when they're talking; it can sound like code to an outsider, although really it's just that they know each other so well that they can follow each other.<br /> <br /> After her mother's death, Delphine learnt to detach herself from her feelings and just cope. She's definitely stronger for it, but it does mean that she doesn't always take things as seriously as perhaps she should. She's very pretty, and although she's a good kid, she's learnt how to make use of her looks when needs be. She used to get a load of spiteful bullshit at school until she started fighting back, and now she is a social force to be reckoned with, particularly as she is perceptive about people. Delphine is outgoing, with a generous heart, a good sense of fun, and a total lack of respect for petty authority, so she is popular with just about everyone. Even the bitch squad has twigged that she is a lot more fun to hang with than to have as an enemy. Besides which, there are effectively two of her...<br /> <br /> Delphine and her sister are on the school swimming and athletics teams, and have repeatedly turned down offers to join the cheer squad, mainly because they don't have time. Their grades are good but not spectacular; they tend to coast their school work, relying on intelligence to pull them through. Delphine has a strong unconventional streak, and is perfectly happy making friends right across the school social structure. She's had a number of boyfriends, but nothing serious. Her tastes veer to the alternative -- she's more into Avril Lavigne, Feeder and the Foo Fighters than Britney, Christina or Enrique, and she thinks Johnny Depp is just way too cute. She's been meaning to get good with the guitar for a couple of years now. She can play a bit, but not enough, and she's got a great singing voice, so she reckons it's a shame not to give it a try. Deep down, she wants to be adored by everyone.<br /> <br /> Her dad is a little distant, and although they're close, she finds him tricky to talk to sometimes. She helps out around the house as much as possible, and tries to pretend that she doesn't notice when he has a bad night. He hasn't had a serious relationship since her mom died, and although she was jealously glad of that when she was younger, she's getting kinda worried about it now.<br /> <br /> Delphine hasn't really thought too much about what she wants from the future; if she can't make it as a star -- which she doesn't really expect to, but wants to try -- then she figures something will come up. Which it will. Just not quite in the way she was expecting...<br /> <br /> <br /> DELPHINE'S STATS<br /> <br /> Clan: Brujah<br /> Sire: Kristine<br /> Nature: Survivor<br /> Demeanor: Gallant<br /> Generation: 8th<br /> Embrace: 2002<br /> Apparent Age: 17<br /> <br /> Physical: Strength 1, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2<br /> Social: Charisma 4, Manipulation 4, Appearance 4<br /> Mental: Perception 4, Intelligence 3, Wits 2<br /> <br /> Talents: Alertness 2, Athletics 2, Dodge 1, Empathy 3, Expression 2, Subterfuge 4<br /> Skills: Animal Ken 1, Drive 1, Etiquette 1, Firearms 2, Melee 1, Performance 4<br /> Knowledges: Academ 1, Computer 3, Politics 1<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Fortitude 1, Potence 1, Presence 1<br /> Backgrounds: Generation 5, Mentor 4 (theo)<br /> <br /> Virtues: Conscience 3, Self-Control 3, Courage 5<br /> Morality: Humanity 7<br /> Derangements: None<br /> Flaws: Prey Exclusion - Teenage Girls, Vengeful, Infamous Sire<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> <br /> <br /> -o-<br /> <br /> ITIO'S STATS<br /> <br /> Clan: Malkavian<br /> Sire: Lucius<br /> Nature: Explorer<br /> Demeanor: Mentor<br /> Generation: 7th<br /> Embrace: 1787<br /> Apparent Age: mid 30s<br /> <br /> Physical: Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 4<br /> Social: Charisma 4, Manipulation 5, Appearance 4<br /> Mental: Perception 6, Intelligence 5, Wits 5<br /> <br /> Talents: Alertness 4, Atheltics 2, Brawl 3, Dodge 2, Empathy 2, Grace 2, Intimidation 1, Intuition 5, Malkavian Time 5, Streetwise 4, Style 2, Subterfuge 3<br /> Skills: Animal Ken 2, Demolitions 2, Disguise 4, Drive 3, Etiquette 2, Firearms 4, Lip-reading 1, Melee 4, Performance 1, Security 5, Stealth 5, Survival 4<br /> Knowledges: Academ 5, Bureaucracy 3, Camarila Lore 4, Enigmas 5, Finance 2, Investigation 5, Kindred Lore 4, Law 3, Linguistics 5, Occult 5, Politics 2, Science 2, Underworld Lore 3<br /> <br /> Disciplines: Auspex 4, Dementation 6, Dominate 5, Fortitude 1, Hedge Magic, Necromancy 2, Obfuscate 5, Protean 3<br /> Backgrounds: Allies 5, Contacts 5, Herd 4, Influence 3, Resources 4<br /> <br /> Virtues: Conscience 4, Self-Control 4, Courage 5<br /> Morality: Humanity 5<br /> Derangements: Sanguinary Animism<br /> Willpower: 8<br /> <br /> -o-<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 07-23-2020, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T12:02:52-07:00","id":1404272,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1594_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1594\" data-vbnamecard=\"1594\">Saga</a>: Thanks for the insight. I agree the Brujah Trilogy was one of the best pieces of WoD fiction written, filled with cool moments (Theo and Xaviar vs Karsh is one of my favored... despite them winning in the end you can see how outmatched they really are and we are talking about one of the most powerful archons out there and an ex Justicar! Whne Iread it I realized how well the author knew these characters even from the mechanical point of view).<br /> <br /> Btw, what makes you think the VtM writers of the time disliked the Brujah Trilogy? It was in perfect continuity with the Gehenna novel and V5 basically keeps the events presented within (Theo growing disillusioned with the Camarilla to mention one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-19T08:01:49-08:00","id":1472779,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1594_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1594\" data-vbnamecard=\"1594\">Saga</a> : A note about Carnell the Overseer: He is most likely Baali rather than Malkavian. He uses what is clearly Daimonion 1 to sense the weaknesses of his targets with supernatural precision; he uses Balefire with Daimonion 3, and he uses Daimonion 2 to terrify and unhinge his targets with their greatest fears. He is also uber-evil beyond the other typical villains. Yet we see his internal monologue, and he doesn't show any insanity there. He has demonic investments, and these abilities could come from Dark Thaumaturgy as well as Daimonion; but the way he uses his abilities instinctively rather than with invocations suggests the latter as more likely. He could be a vampire from another clan who learned Daimonion, but I think a Baali is most likely.<br /> <br /> As for the two puppet masters, I think they are most likely standard Brujah rather than True Brujah. We don't get to see the female infernalist's internal dialogue, but Rodrigo is immensely irritable and prone to frenzy. He fights with elder levels of Celerity and Potence and could not be outfought by multiple opponents with these Disciplines. He makes comments about how far the Brujah have fallen, but he seems to take it personally rather than reveling in it. His partner also fights with elder Potence. My guess is that he at least is an elder Brujah infernalist (we know that the Path of Evil Revelations was publicized in the past by Iberian Brujah).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13688-sultanabdal","name":"Sultanabdal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13688_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T08:22:39-08:00","id":1472878,"title":"","content":"Wasn't Karsh / Jalan-Aajav implied to be one of the Seraphs of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, or was I under that impression because Jalan-Aajav was one of the 4 Seraphim of the Sabbat's Black Hand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T12:38:13-08:00","id":1472897,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">My 2 cts.<br /> <br /> JA\u2019s reported destruction in V5 can be considered as in-character knowledge. (Since we only see it mentioned in a note written in game)<br /> I wouldn\u2019t consider that as fact.<br /> Even if someone/something was destroyed, no way of knowing it was K/JA. The SI may believe it was JA or they may even be lying about the whole thing.<br /> <br /> Assuming K and JA are split forms:<br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">We don\u2019t know how Dual form actually works.<br /> Can both forms act independently? For how long? Is it permanent? Do they develop different traits over time?<br /> And indeed, \u201cwhat happens if one of them dies\u201d<br /> Maybe both forms rejoin and we now have a reformed Qarakh on the loose\u2026.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <i>edit: So I've looked up the mechanics for dual form.<br /> My bad, I should've written &quot;I don't know how Dual form works&quot;, or even better, looked it up beforehand.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">BTW, Karsh being staked in the trilogy means nothing.<br /> He has/had access to protean lvl 8 (pre V5 of course, when the trilogy was written)<br /> It\u2019s not inconceivable that would have been the power \u2018<span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Purify the Impaled Breast\u2019.<br /> I would actually be surprised if he didn\u2019t have it. I always found it far-fetched he even got bested. Fortitude 7, try rolling that fight on the table.<br /> Admittedly it\u2019s unlikely that a figure like him would play it smart and not come back for revenge, but who knows, he was being puppeteered after all.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#3A3A3A\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Assuming they are/were the same guy:<br /> If K was a puppet then so was JA?<br /> A terribly convoluted way to be \u2018running the show\u2019 so to speak, in the Sabbat, yet be the Camarilla warlord at the same time.</span></span><br /> Not impossible but implausible. Especially for a combat oriented slaying deathmachine, maybe less so for a genius manipulator.<br /> That also means that if the trilogy did happen, K/JA would have survived the staking, but not the SI\u2019s attack.<br /> (Or he did. Two near destructions, that would be my clue to disappear for a while\u2026)<br /> I do feel this fits better within V5, but I don\u2019t buy it.<br /> <br /> My money is on door no 1 but we\u2019ll likely never get the answers. It\u2019s all left purposefully hazy so we can speculate and use it to our own liking.</span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","user":"Moriaki","date":". 01-25-2022, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T14:32:29-08:00","id":1472905,"title":"","content":"We know how dual form works, its in Players Guide Second edition page 80. It has mechanics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3215-supersabbatst","name":"SuperSabbatST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"196"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-20T14:42:32-08:00","id":1472906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1472878#post1472878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't Karsh / Jalan-Aajav implied to be one of the Seraphs of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, or was I under that impression because Jalan-Aajav was one of the 4 Seraphim of the Sabbat's Black Hand?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was the only modern Black Hand Seraph that wasn't in the know about the Tal'Mahe'Ra. Well, until he found out in <i>Caine's Chosen: The Black Hand</i> after the disappearance of the other three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-21T11:12:39-08:00","id":1472984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1282946#post1282946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I maintain that Karsh and Jalan are the same character but rather than the Protean 9 split, it was more the two made use of a lot of body doubles and Obfuscate-capable minions.<br /> <br /> So are they dead?<br /> <br /> Who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I honestly treat that as one of many &quot;near endgame twists &quot; pulled for their own sake in Revised era because no one truly gave a damn about the original NPCs.<br /> Karsh and Jalan-Aajav as the same person <i><b>doesn't make any sense whatsoever</b></i> beyond &quot;<i>ah, they were both Gangrel and medieval soldiers, make tots sense to make them the same person!</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> No, it doesn't - Jalan-Aajav was a small unit light cavalry &amp; archery officer, basically a lieutenant <i>at most</i>, among the mongol hordes of the time of Gengis Khan. Plus, he is very much lampshaded as a crap uncharismatic leader that raised in the social pyramid through seniority, secret illegal bonding &amp; assassination (plus under-the-table deals with <b>Genevra's faction</b> within the Giovanni, <i>the ones with Inquisition ties that would sacrifice rivals to the hunters</i>).<br /> Karsh was a Janissary general of the Ottoman Empire betrayed by court intrigues and the pettiness of his sultan, in the 1600s. Also, he was handpicked <b>for </b>his role of Camarilla war leader, pretty much embraced into the elite like Jan Pieterzoon though of a different clan and focus, what says much of his strategic and political accumen for the period that he was targeted in such a manner.<br /> <br /> Quite different tier of their respective pecking orders, quite different era of war, not to mention cultural background.<br /> <i>It only gets <b>more</b> nonsensical</i> if one adds <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Qarakh\" target=\"_blank\">Qarakh</a> to the mix as some fan theories try - because that one <b><i>is an almost platonic diametrical opposite</i></b> of what Jalan-Aajav is supposed to be, even thought coming from the same era and culture.<br /> <br /> <br /> Seriously, the quantity of inconsistencies if one cares to decently read on their original portrayals, even though statless, is mind-boggling. If one needs some evil ancient secret puppetmaster to hide under both their faces, just say it's Izhim Ur-Baal trolling the hell out of everybody.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-21-2022, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-22T14:23:30-08:00","id":1473044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1472878#post1472878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't Karsh / Jalan-Aajav implied to be one of the Seraphs of the Tal'Mahe'Ra, or was I under that impression because Jalan-Aajav was one of the 4 Seraphim of the Sabbat's Black Hand?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Brujah trilogy strongly implies that Karsh / Jalan-Aajav are one and the same. After Theo and Xaviar send Karsh to the bottom of the ocean Jalan-Aajav we learn that the Sabbat stopped being able to make contact with their Seraph, which was a nice way to hint at the theory that Karsh was actually Jalan-Aajav (having the exact same stats).<br /> <br /> @<b>Baaldam: </b>The theory goes like this. Karsh and Jalan-Aajav are proxy identities of Qarakh (the signature character for DA:V Gangrel). A strategy he developed after him diablerizing Alexander and the destruction of the Telyavelic Tremere (which included Deverra, thus fulfilling the condition needed for him to safely leave Livonia). The question is how and why he decided to work for the &quot;puppet masters&quot;, which apparently were his masters and were even more powerful than him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 01-22-2022, 05:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T10:56:30-08:00","id":1473086,"title":"","content":"...The SI killed Jalan-Aajav? The guy who, according to the wiki, has this among his stats:<br /> <b>physical Strength 8, Dexterity 7, Stamina 8</b><br /> <br /> <b>mental Perception 7, Intelligence 6, Wits 7</b><br /> <br /> <b>disciplines <b>Animalism 4, Auspex 1, <u>Celerity 7</u>, Dominate 1, <u>Fortitude 7</u>, <u>Potence 6</u>, Presence 2, <u>Protean 8</u></b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> They better have ganked him at high noon, or I'm calling bull**** on them being able to do it without the fight causing a ruckus large enough to feature on prime time tv.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1631-karthak","name":"Karthak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1631_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T11:38:22-08:00","id":1473091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karthak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1473086#post1473086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...The SI killed Jalan-Aajav? The guy who, according to the wiki, has this among his stats:<br /> <b>physical Strength 8, Dexterity 7, Stamina 8</b><br /> <br /> <b>mental Perception 7, Intelligence 6, Wits 7</b><br /> <br /> <b>disciplines <b>Animalism 4, Auspex 1, <u>Celerity 7</u>, Dominate 1, <u>Fortitude 7</u>, <u>Potence 6</u>, Presence 2, <u>Protean 8</u></b></b><br /> <br /> <br /> They better have ganked him at high noon, or I'm calling bull**** on them being able to do it without the fight causing a ruckus large enough to feature on prime time tv.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;SI killed Jalan-Aajav&quot; is not a &quot;fact&quot; it's a rumor. Given how obscure and difficult to verify things are in the WoD it might very well be JA had been &quot;dead&quot; for quite a long time and the SI was blamed for his disappearance despite having nothing to do with it because the SI was being treated as some impossibly powerful bogeyman.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-23T21:20:54-08:00","id":1473140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1473091#post1473091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;SI killed Jalan-Aajav&quot; is not a &quot;fact&quot; it's a rumor. Given how obscure and difficult to verify things are in the WoD it might very well be JA had been &quot;dead&quot; for quite a long time and the SI was blamed for his disappearance despite having nothing to do with it because the SI was being treated as some impossibly powerful bogeyman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, also, are we really assuming the Second Inquisition would FIGHT Jalan?<br /> <br /> I mean, how stupid do we think the Inquisitors are?<br /> <br /> Am I the only one who believes vampire hunters are dangerous because they're smart enough to do the Alfred thing?<br /> <br /> &quot;Did you ever catch the bandit?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;How?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We burned the forest down.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm presuming that if Jalan is dead, it's because he was in a non-American country when his car was hit by a drone strike. Either that or he was in America and they covered up said drone strike.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T06:35:02-08:00","id":1473162,"title":"","content":"V5 Core said Jalan Ajaav was more victim of the War on Terror than of the Second Inquisition: he was struck down as the US Government thought he was a linkage between Mexican drug cartels and Al Quaeda, and it says he killed 14 operatives.<br /> <br /> They probably sent some Delta Force to kill him, and when he simply shrugged off bullets and started killing Marines, they drone-bombed him, until he got ashed.<br /> <br /> In fact, I suppose the battle with Jalan was the thing that probably triggered a phone call to SAD by higher ups in the US secret service, saying &quot;<i>Ooook ... perhaps you were right about monsters in the night. Let's discuss</i>&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 01-24-2022, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-24T20:05:38-08:00","id":1473226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1472984#post1472984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly treat that as one of many &quot;near endgame twists &quot; pulled for their own sake in Revised era because no one truly gave a damn about the original NPCs.<br /> Karsh and Jalan-Aajav as the same person <i><b>doesn't make any sense whatsoever</b></i> beyond &quot;<i>ah, they were both Gangrel and medieval soldiers, make tots sense to make them the same person!</i>&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, here's the problem, you're looking at it from the perspective of LOGIC.<br /> <br /> When I'm looking at it from the perspective of <u>sheer insanity.</u><br /> <br /> Specifically, the idea that there is a 5th Generation Gangrel Methuselah out there who is running both sides of the Camarilla and Sabbat sect war <i>just for the hell of of it.</i> It was a bit more of a concept before Darth Sidious was a thing but the whole idea is just so ridiculously insane that you almost want it to be true just because.<br /> <br /> Forget the specifics of his backstory, think about just what sort of psychology and lengths someone would have to go to in order to pull this off. A guy presumably with Nosferatu, fleshcrafted body doubles, Tzimisce agents, and proxies that are all doing this guys bidding as well as what his higher end is.<br /> <br /> Because it's very likely THERE IS NO HIGHER END. That Jalav/Karsh created this massive war between the two sects and constantly feeds it because he's a Kindred warrior and the time of the Kindred warrior has passed. Because if not for him and others like him, the Camarilla and Sabbat would fight solely through proxies or influence.<br /> <br /> So he made an eternal unending conflict between the sects solely so there would be a place for him and vampires like him he didn't want to sip tea and rule from the shadows.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>We will forsake our countries. We will leave our motherlands behind us and become one with this earth. We have no nation, no philosophy, no ideology. We go where we're needed, fighting, not for government, but for ourselves. We need no reason to fight. We fight because we are needed. We will be the deterrent for those with no other recourse. We are soldiers without borders, our purpose defined by the era we live in. We will sometimes have to sell ourselves and services. If the times demand it, we'll be revolutionaries, criminals, terrorists. And yes, we may all be headed straight to hell. But what better place for us than this? It's our only home. Our heaven and our hell. This is Outer Heaven. </i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-24-2022, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T00:02:32-08:00","id":1473237,"title":"","content":"And Jalan is not even a True Black Hand guy - at least they truly are ideologically committed to fostering war between Kindred!<br /> <br /> Of course, Karsh instead really looks like a TBH dupe ... so if they are the same, Jalan may be unaware of the true loyalty of his Other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 01-25-2022, 03:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T03:26:01-08:00","id":1473243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1473226#post1473226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now, here's the problem, you're looking at it from the perspective of LOGIC.<br /> <br /> When I'm looking at it from the perspective of <u>sheer insanity.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>No, i'm looking at the perspective of someone who has seen 2-3 characters that he appreciated each in its own way retconned into &quot;<b><i>Masks of Cartoonhotep</i></b>&quot;, aka cover identities of just another uberpuppetmaster meth with no real character or story beyond &quot;i need an excuse for my Darth Sidious style plotting!&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, not particularly entused and gushing at the <i>inventiveness</i> of it all.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 01-25-2022, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T05:09:48-08:00","id":1473249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1473140#post1473140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, also, are we really assuming the Second Inquisition would FIGHT Jalan?<br /> <br /> I mean, how stupid do we think the Inquisitors are?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:arial\">As stupid as a 9th gen Brujah and a 7th gen Gangrel?<br /> But of course inquisitors do not have the 'Bell always wins' perk on their stat sheets...</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-25T08:48:09-08:00","id":1473265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moriaki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1473249#post1473249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">As stupid as a 9th gen Brujah and a 7th gen Gangrel?<br /> But of course inquisitors do not have the 'Bell always wins' perk on their stat sheets...</span></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I still remember when my players attacked a DRAMATICALLY overpowered vampire and the latter Botched their Dominate use.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1473243#post1473243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, i'm looking at the perspective of someone who has seen 2-3 characters that he appreciated each in its own way retconned into &quot;<b><i>Masks of Cartoonhotep</i></b>&quot;, aka cover identities of just another uberpuppetmaster meth with no real character or story beyond &quot;i need an excuse for my Darth Sidious style plotting!&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah, not particularly entused and gushing at the <i>inventiveness</i> of it all.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think Darth Sidious puppetmastering is the wrong thing to disdain in a game about playing the undead Illuminati. Its not really getting into the spirit of things.<br /> <br /> V:TM is *THE* game of manipulating behind the scenes, treachery, and lies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T12:34:32-08:00","id":1473540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moriaki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1473249#post1473249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">As stupid as a 9th gen Brujah and a 7th gen Gangrel?<br /> But of course inquisitors do not have the 'Bell always wins' perk on their stat sheets...</span></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, if you read the chapter they fight Xaviar and TB taking down Karsh is actually believable. And yes, TB has killed/defeated a number of methuselahs at this point and it got abit silly, but he's also always been one of those characters who manage to triumph despite the odds, it's not like he just marched in and killed Vitel, Karsh, the puppetmasters and Hardestadt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T04:04:01-08:00","id":1473562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1473540#post1473540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> it's not like he just marched in and killed Vitel, Karsh, the puppetmasters and Hardestadt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, that's exactly what he did.<br /> Roll those fights on the tabletop and see how many (adversary) botches you'll need to actually survive, let alone win. Do this 4 times.<br /> Hardestadt? Ok, I'll buy it.<br /> The others? I'm sorry but that's beyond credible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-05T16:19:15-08:00","id":1474059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moriaki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1282916-karsh-in-v5?p=1473562#post1473562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually, that's exactly what he did.<br /> Roll those fights on the tabletop and see how many (adversary) botches you'll need to actually survive, let alone win. Do this 4 times.<br /> Hardestadt? Ok, I'll buy it.<br /> The others? I'm sorry but that's beyond credible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Listen man, it's Gherbod Flemings campaign. He can run the game how he wants!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-06T09:27:36-08:00","id":1474081,"title":"","content":"Pretty much my Personal Point of View, but I don't think or actually like the idea of Karsh and Jalav and Qarakh actually being the same. And it is my own position on it, but I don't base lore questions on the endless 6+ Disciplines powers, ever; I don't know, I just think it's too shaky a ground to base things off; the exceptions are when it is used in-canon.<br /> <br /> I didn't read the novels to know how Xaviar and Bell got to jump up the Warlord, but well, the writer will have what the writer wants, so although I think it would've needed more powerful people and much more planning, it can be done. I just don't know what does this do for the setting.<br /> <br /> Theo Bell being an Elder Wrecking Ball is a bit funny, especially in the WoD, where every ancient vampire wouldn't let this get any mile closer and would probably just off him if possible (if not for being a threat, for being an elder-killing icon, which he kind is). And yet, I still think Hardestadt, through whatever scheme (willingly or not) had Bell do what he did; and maybe make him such an ancient killer was all part of decades of planning. <br /> I mean... the Camarilla was only possible after Tyler attempted on his life (one of them let's say). So, in this new time of crisis, being destroyed in the middle of a Conclave, could be exactly the shaking that the sect needed, at least in Hardestadt's eyes. He will conquer 'from the grave' said his motto. <br /> <br /> So... I guess Karsh, Xaviar, Hardestadt, Jalav and many others are simply wiped out to follow the V5 dogma of an &quot;Elder Free-ish&quot; setting (if not &quot;Elder Rare&quot;). Too many godlike figures, and the Tal'Mahe'Ra was a sect of just that, so they are now either spread out and not working together, or really are out of the game. Thing is, where are either not gonna hear from them again, or only in a second or third period of this edition's life. Although this isn't much of a real issue with me, I'm really lore-hungry, especially about the characters, so I would love to hear about what happened.<br /> Maybe in the Second Coming of Becket's Jyhad Diary or some such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}